# Repo-root Docker build context exclusions (packaging/docker/Dockerfile,
# T43A3). Keep every workspace package.json, package-lock.json, and every
# package/app's src/ — the build stage runs `npm ci` and the full workspace
# build chain from this context.
#
# Docker's ignore-pattern matcher anchors a pattern to the CONTEXT ROOT
# unless it starts with `**/`: `node_modules/` (no leading `**/`) excludes
# only `./node_modules`, never `apps/web/node_modules` or any other
# workspace's own copy. This is an npm-workspaces repo, so `node_modules`,
# `dist`, `*.log` and `*.tsbuildinfo` are all produced inside every
# package and app directory, not only at the root — T177 gave those four
# patterns the `**/` prefix they need, after finding they had silently
# stayed root-only since T43A3 first wrote this file (`docs/issues-from-
# plan.md` T177 has the re-measurement: at the time of that fix six
# nested workspace `node_modules` directories, ten nested `dist`
# directories and two nested `.tsbuildinfo` files were entering the build
# context unexcluded — none of them carrying a native `.node` binary; all
# 15 in this tree live under the root `node_modules`, which
# `**/node_modules/` still excludes, so the fix was about context
# accuracy and size, not a broken image). Everything below is either a
# build artifact the image rebuilds from scratch, host-platform-specific
# `node_modules` that must never be copied into the Linux build stage at
# ANY depth (see packaging/docker/Dockerfile's stage-1 comment on native
# module platform/arch resolution), or scratch/tooling output the image
# has no use for.

**/node_modules/
**/dist/
.git/
# T180: `.github/` is NOT root-only "by construction" as this file's T177
# commit message claimed — `packages/expo-two-way-audio/.github/workflows/`
# is a real, tracked, nested `.github` directory (leftover CI config from
# the AGPL-ported upstream package; scripts/ci/guard-dockerignore-depth.mjs
# found it as real on-disk evidence, not the built-artifact kind). `**/`
# added so this actually excludes it too.
**/.github/
.dev/
.tmp/
.pi/
.expo/
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Playwright E2E run artifacts. Playwright's default `outputDir`/report
# locations are relative to its config file, not the repo root, so these
# land under apps/web/e2e/ (T31A) — same root-anchoring pitfall as above,
# so these need `**/` too.
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/

# Expo/Android native prebuild output (apps/android; T16) — Android is not
# part of the daemon image.
apps/android/.expo/
apps/android/android/
apps/android/ios/
# Metro writes its health-check file into the Expo project root
# (apps/android/), not the repo root, so this also needs `**/`.
**/.metro-health-check*

# Agent scratch and handoff documents not needed to build the daemon image.
HANDOFF.md
claude-code-handoff.md
memory.md
